# Teaching readiness — FE I / FE II, curso 2026-27

**Re-audited 2026-08-28** against the current lesson sources, track registry, gap pass, fresh local build, generated-asset operations, and Ahmes 12H formula-readiness reports.

## 0. Current verdict

**FE I: curriculum-ready; delivery sign-off remains.** The 29-session sequence is indexed, its official 10/30/14 activity allocation closes, and its canonical lessons are publicly navigable in the local build.

**FE II: no longer an essay-only scaffold.** All 12 units now have a student lesson, individual-exercise file, deck outline, master-idea/field-lens framing, semantic graphic, outcome illustration, and a session outcome. Ten code-bearing units contain 77 labelled code fences in total. Units 1 and 12 intentionally have no runnable code because they are orientation and oral-defence units.

**FE II teaching: ready for instructor technical rehearsal, not automatic release.** The remaining teaching risk is runtime verification, lab-machine access, assessment freezing, and delivery logistics—not missing lesson prose.

**Research: blocked.** The assessment traces exist, but consent, DPO approval, independent administration, retention rules, and frozen instrument versions do not.

**Pilot status remains real.** Astro/islands, PWA failure-mode teaching, performance pedagogy, R3F, minimum GLSL, and FE-to-device transfer have bounded precedents but no direct validation of these exact sequences.

