### P2 — scholarly gaps; keep the pilot honest

These gaps do **not** block teaching after P0. They block stronger claims.

| Unit(s) | Current boundary | Next evidence work | Allowed claim now |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 2–3 Astro/islands | Safe rendering/architecture technique; no direct HE comparison of Astro/islands sequences | Search comparative metaframework teaching or transfer studies | Transfer-informed pilot; assess boundary decisions |
| 4 PWA/offline | Safe offline-first architecture; adjacent school case only | Seek FE/HE intervention evidence with recovery-state tasks | Failure-mode pilot; no checklist-as-learning claim |
| 7 Performance | Normative responsibility and sector vocabulary; performance pedagogy and empirical front-end-to-carbon effect remain open | Resolve source metadata and seek measured pedagogy/energy work | Evidence-based measurement practice, not carbon-effect proof |
| 8 R3F | Safe concept-first graphics precedent; no R3F-specific pedagogy | Seek API-transfer or declarative-graphics teaching studies | Graphics-grounded pilot |
| 9 Shaders | Safe graphics/API-churn precedent; no validated minimum-GLSL sequence | Seek shader literacy and transfer assessment studies | Classroom contract, not validated syllabus |
| 10 IoT/interface | Safe IoT curriculum/interface-layer review; no FE component/state → Python/device transfer study | Seek transfer studies that isolate the interface layer | Transfer pilot; assess telemetry-to-decision reasoning |
| FE I React | Strong curriculum content; secondary gap in direct HE component-pedagogy depth | Run only if making comparative learning-effect claims | Teach the established sequence without causal claim |

For every evidence upgrade:

1. Use `profield-frontend-pedagogy` or the named specialty field for discovery.
2. Treat vector results and current vendor docs as leads/HOW, not scholarly evidence.
3. Read the complete Ahmes node and page context.
4. Require `evaluator_safe=yes` before adding a public Chicago citation.
5. Keep unresolved Ciungan, AI Co-Artist, MCP/preprint, host-title, and other records quarantined as `[BIBLIO-GAP]`; never repair them by inference.
6. Update the evidence matrix, lesson boundary, References section, and this readiness table together.

### P0-R — research/data governance

Teaching may proceed without this section. Research data collection may not.

- [ ] Create `frontend-pedagogy/research-line/` with protocol, consent forms, instrument versions, data dictionary, retention schedule, and ethics correspondence.
- [ ] Name the controller, processors/storage, lawful basis, retention period, withdrawal route, deletion deadline, and pseudonymisation boundary.
- [ ] Obtain UDIT DPO sign-off and clarify whether institutional ethics review is required.
- [ ] Add UEM approval only if the cross-institutional synergy/data stream is in the protocol.
- [ ] Have the sociologist/independent custodian administer consent; participation must be grade-neutral and hidden from the instructor until final grades are filed.
- [ ] Freeze and date the AI-use declaration, oral-defence rubric, decision log, iteration log, and review-log schema before collection.
- [ ] Decide the minimum dataset. Do not collect repository history, declarations, recordings, surveys, or interviews merely because they exist.
- [ ] Validate entry/exit survey scales; do not invent psychometrics.
- [ ] Define interview/focus-group sampling, recording, transcription, access, and deletion procedures.
- [ ] Record the “no consent, no research dataset” fallback before teaching begins.

If P0-R is incomplete when the course starts, run the course as teaching only. Do not retroactively convert graded work into research data.

## 3. Release acceptance checklist

- [ ] `npm run build` performs a clean build and passes publication/citation checks.
- [ ] If generated graphics were refreshed, the previous SVG/PNG/manifest set remains recoverable from the archive folder.
- [ ] Formula-driven artwork uses only exportable Ahmes formula glossary records, not vector snippets or unverified `normalized_text`.
- [ ] FE I and FE II track pages expose every intended lesson link.
- [ ] Every canonical lesson has exactly one semantic and one outcome figure.
- [ ] No internal corpus name, resolver status, node/coat ID, local path, or source-only comment appears in `_site`.
- [ ] Public author-date citations have a final References section.
- [ ] Runtime examples pass the technical smoke matrix on the teaching environment.
- [ ] Assessment instrument version and release/tag are recorded in the Campus Virtual.
- [ ] Public pages make pilot boundaries explicit and contain no promised learning effect unsupported by evidence.

## 4. Meaning of “done”

- **Ready to teach FE I:** P0 complete for the FE I delivery environment.
- **Ready to teach FE II:** P0 plus the technical smoke matrix complete.
- **Ready as a polished pack:** selected P1 handouts/decks/starters complete.
- **Ready to study:** every P0-R item complete before collection.
- **Evidence-complete:** not required; the declared frontier is part of the curriculum, provided its claims remain bounded.
